diff --git a/docs/configuration.md b/docs/configuration.md
index 1954cb64d1fe1cbe4949a3200bdb72f40523e0cf..430cf95100eea5ee1e178157844526b7f9173154 100644
--- a/docs/configuration.md
+++ b/docs/configuration.md
@@ -18,6 +18,20 @@ npx bb-app config refresh
 
 Use `bb-app env` for provider credentials and provider-specific environment:
 
+`CODEX_APP_SERVER_EXECUTABLE` selects an absolute executable for all native
+Codex app-server children (sessions, model listing and maintenance). Set it
+with `bb-app env set CODEX_APP_SERVER_EXECUTABLE /absolute/router-command` on
+the execution host, then restart that host's BB launcher and daemon. Server
+configuration refresh and `bb thread stop` alone do not update the daemon's
+inherited environment. This is host-local policy, not a server setting sent to
+remote daemons. After restart, prove fresh start and resume on that host. The
+bridge passes `app-server` as its sole argument. A missing, non-executable,
+empty or relative selection fails closed; it never falls back to PATH. When
+unset, Codex retains its default `codex app-server` PATH lookup. Version-manager
+reshimming cannot change an explicitly selected launcher. This setting does
+not alter account homes, credentials or already-running processes. The
+`BB_CODEX_BRIDGE_APP_SERVER_*` variables remain test-only, not host policy.
+
 ```bash
 npx bb-app env set OPENAI_API_KEY <key>
 npx bb-app env list
